BT 1 0 0 1 0 63.6 Tm /F3 12 Tf 15.12 TL (This is reactive installation: traffic that misses a rule prompts the controller to act. A proactive) Tj T* (implementation can populate rules before the relevant data packet arrives. The project also uses) Tj T* (this approach when installing forwarding along a known host path. Reactive handling saves space) Tj T* (for unused pairs but costs control messages and first-packet latency. Proactive installation trades) Tj T* (earlier work and table space for faster handling of expected traffic.) Tj T* ET
